WEBVTT

00:49.049 --> 00:51.969
ALL CHARACTERS, INCIDENTS, ORGANIZATIONS,
AND BACKGROUND ARE FICTITIOUS

00:57.599 --> 00:59.643
I told you not to come.

01:00.352 --> 01:02.604
I don't want you to see my face.

01:09.069 --> 01:10.237
Next year,

01:11.446 --> 01:12.698
the year after that,

01:14.700 --> 01:15.993
and even the one after that

01:18.328 --> 01:19.705
will all be good.

01:22.165 --> 01:24.084
Because I'll be thinking about you.

01:25.627 --> 01:27.713
I'll be grateful that you were born
into this world.

01:30.007 --> 01:31.258
I'll be grateful

01:33.427 --> 01:36.596
that the person I love is still breathing.

01:39.391 --> 01:41.059
That's why your birthday

01:42.686 --> 01:44.313
will always be a good day.

02:21.433 --> 02:23.185
I thought you had left.

02:24.353 --> 02:26.772
Are you planning to cry like that
once I leave?

02:27.898 --> 02:29.650
No one plans to cry.

02:30.859 --> 02:32.903
Tears come unexpectedly.

02:34.488 --> 02:36.990
I don't want you to cry alone.

02:37.658 --> 02:40.452
Since I cried today, I won't do it again.

02:41.495 --> 02:43.121
I got vaccinated just now.

02:52.798 --> 02:53.882
I heard

02:54.925 --> 02:56.176
by chance.

02:57.677 --> 02:58.762
Stop making things

03:00.639 --> 03:02.349
hard for your father

03:03.308 --> 03:04.434
and go back.

03:05.102 --> 03:06.895
I will take care of that matter.

03:08.814 --> 03:12.275
There is something called
the Bambi Syndrome.

03:14.694 --> 03:16.863
When a baby deer

03:17.989 --> 03:19.866
meets people in the mountains,

03:21.993 --> 03:25.330
people pet it saying it's so cute.

03:25.664 --> 03:27.541
But once people leave,

03:28.750 --> 03:30.085
the baby deer

03:30.794 --> 03:33.422
can't go back to its family.

03:34.840 --> 03:36.216
Due to the smell

03:38.051 --> 03:39.928
of people on its body,

03:40.929 --> 03:41.972
its family

03:42.180 --> 03:43.473
rejects it.

03:44.933 --> 03:47.310
The baby deer
that is rejected from its group

03:49.020 --> 03:50.605
dies in the end.

03:54.192 --> 03:55.235
Are you worried

03:56.027 --> 03:59.489
that I will be rejected and abandoned

04:00.365 --> 04:01.867
by my group?

04:02.534 --> 04:04.202
I will protect myself.

04:04.995 --> 04:06.538
Believe in me.

04:07.914 --> 04:09.249
In my world,

04:10.167 --> 04:15.338
I will use my status, people, money,
and everything else.

04:15.839 --> 04:17.215
Cho Cheol Gang...

04:18.258 --> 04:19.134
No.

04:19.843 --> 04:21.595
No one will be able

04:23.221 --> 04:24.931
to take me down.

04:25.682 --> 04:27.142
Believe in me...

04:29.853 --> 04:32.022
and go back, Jeong Hyeok.

04:35.358 --> 04:36.860
Go back to your world.

04:47.329 --> 04:50.290
Wasn't it the first time she cried?

04:50.373 --> 04:51.625
You are right.

04:51.708 --> 04:54.294
Even when she crossed the ceasefire line,
she didn't cry.

04:54.377 --> 04:57.297
Even when she got caught
on the smuggling boat, she didn't cry.

04:58.298 --> 05:00.801
And even when she failed to escape
through the airport,

05:01.593 --> 05:02.594
she didn't cry.

05:07.265 --> 05:09.100
Just how much did you listen in on us?

05:14.523 --> 05:15.941
Why aren't they coming back?

05:16.024 --> 05:20.362
I hope the two of them just run away!

05:22.155 --> 05:24.199
Don't say something so dangerous.

05:24.282 --> 05:26.952
Military World Games will be over
in a few days.

05:27.035 --> 05:30.455
We must go back with Jeong Hyeok
before then.

05:31.665 --> 05:32.874
I am sorry.

05:33.208 --> 05:36.628
She didn't even blink
when I told her that I will bury her.

05:36.711 --> 05:38.713
Seeing her cry so suddenly

05:39.839 --> 05:40.966
got me flustered.

05:42.551 --> 05:43.885
I will go out for a second.

05:52.936 --> 05:55.188
-What are you doing outside?
-I was worried.

05:55.605 --> 05:56.731
Are you okay?

05:57.315 --> 05:58.441
I am okay.

05:58.525 --> 06:00.235
-Let's go inside.
-Okay.

06:00.318 --> 06:02.404
Everyone is worried and waiting for you.

06:29.889 --> 06:33.226
I got startled because I didn't expect
such an event.

06:34.227 --> 06:36.479
-I am sorry.
-Don't be.

06:37.772 --> 06:40.317
Were you guys worried about me?

06:40.400 --> 06:43.612
Gosh, no one worried about you.

06:44.654 --> 06:46.906
Pyo Chi Su, I didn't expect anything
from you.

06:49.701 --> 06:51.161
Who chose this cake?

06:52.829 --> 06:55.248
Where did you get
such an old-fashioned cake?

07:02.547 --> 07:04.382
-Let's light the candles.
-Okay.

07:05.508 --> 07:06.968
I have only seen this in a drama.

07:07.802 --> 07:10.513
This is my first time
to light candles on a cake.

07:11.806 --> 07:13.558
Let's turn off the light.

07:22.609 --> 07:23.818
All right.

07:24.778 --> 07:25.820
Let's begin.

07:25.904 --> 07:28.657
-Happy birthday, happy birthday
-Happy birthday, happy birthday

07:29.240 --> 07:32.369
-Take this bouquet of flowers
-Take this bouquet of flowers

07:32.494 --> 07:35.580
-Happy birthday, happy birthday
-Happy birthday, happy birthday

07:35.664 --> 07:37.749
-Happy birthday to you
-Happy birthday to you

07:37.832 --> 07:38.792
One more time!

07:38.875 --> 07:41.962
-Happy birthday, happy birthday
-Happy birthday, happy birthday

07:42.045 --> 07:45.090
-Take our blessings
-Take our blessings

07:45.173 --> 07:48.218
-Happy birthday, happy birthday
-Happy birthday, happy birthday

07:48.301 --> 07:51.054
-Happy birthday to you
-Happy birthday to you

07:51.137 --> 07:53.223
-Happy birthday.
-Happy birthday.

07:53.306 --> 07:57.435
I never thought I would hear
the North Korean birthday song.

07:57.686 --> 08:01.064
You know that you need to make a wish

08:01.147 --> 08:03.233
before you blow out the candles, right?

08:05.694 --> 08:07.028
Didn't you know?

08:10.073 --> 08:12.200
I am teaching you so many things.

08:12.283 --> 08:15.620
All right. Close your eyes

08:16.454 --> 08:19.207
and wish for what you want the most.

08:19.874 --> 08:21.751
You blow out the candles after that,

08:21.835 --> 08:23.545
and your wish will come true.

08:35.181 --> 08:36.891
Did you finish making a wish?

08:39.477 --> 08:40.770
Let's blow out the candles.

08:40.854 --> 08:43.189
One, two, three.

08:47.318 --> 08:48.987
Live a good life.

08:49.070 --> 08:50.196
-Happy birthday.
-Thank you.

08:50.280 --> 08:51.823
-Happy birthday.
-Happy birthday.

08:51.906 --> 08:53.324
Thank you, everyone.

09:04.044 --> 09:06.046
EPISODE 13

09:06.463 --> 09:07.714
Come in.

09:10.842 --> 09:12.635
I hope I didn't disturb your rest.

09:13.219 --> 09:14.179
You didn't.

09:15.013 --> 09:16.473
What brings you here?

09:18.349 --> 09:19.434
What is it?

09:20.226 --> 09:21.686
Do you have something for me?

09:21.770 --> 09:22.854
Is it my birthday present?

09:23.521 --> 09:25.106
It's a present,

09:25.690 --> 09:27.025
but it's nothing big.

09:30.570 --> 09:32.781
It doesn't matter. Let me see what it is.

09:33.323 --> 09:34.824
Let me tell you in advance

09:35.241 --> 09:37.577
that this isn't a token of anything.

09:37.869 --> 09:40.872
You don't have to give it
a special meaning.

09:41.456 --> 09:42.999
Okay. I won't do that.

09:43.958 --> 09:46.920
I had to do something for your birthday
when I found out about it.

09:47.545 --> 09:50.215
And I had a bit of free time,

09:51.549 --> 09:53.468
so I bought it.

09:54.135 --> 09:57.806
Although I bought it
without any thoughts...

09:57.889 --> 10:01.476
If you think it's nothing,

10:01.643 --> 10:04.354
you can pawn it.

10:04.771 --> 10:07.315
Are you sweating?

10:09.484 --> 10:11.069
It's hot in here.

10:12.487 --> 10:15.448
Give it to me. Is this your first time
to give a present to a woman?

10:15.532 --> 10:16.699
Why are you so nervous?

10:25.500 --> 10:27.043
It's a ring.

10:31.297 --> 10:34.050
It should fit.

10:39.722 --> 10:41.599
It fits perfectly on my thumb.

10:43.268 --> 10:44.227
That one is mine.

10:46.688 --> 10:47.522
What?

10:56.865 --> 10:59.492
Are these couple's rings?

11:00.076 --> 11:02.537
Is it your first time
to receive a present from a man?

11:03.163 --> 11:06.207
You shouldn't have taken it away from me.
Had you waited a little,

11:08.543 --> 11:10.962
I would have put it on your finger.

11:15.341 --> 11:16.718
Gosh,

11:16.801 --> 11:18.887
when you said you hadn't dated anyone,

11:19.721 --> 11:20.847
I think you were kidding.

11:21.764 --> 11:22.849
Tell me.

11:23.474 --> 11:25.268
Where did you learn this?

11:25.894 --> 11:28.396
Where did you learn
to make a woman's heart flutter?

11:32.734 --> 11:33.776
Give it to me.

11:34.903 --> 11:36.154
Let me do it for you too.

11:52.712 --> 11:53.880
Thank you.

11:57.383 --> 12:00.887
It's the prettiest ring I have ever seen.

12:01.471 --> 12:03.514
I won't take it off
for the rest of my life.

12:05.433 --> 12:06.434
I won't mind if you do.

12:08.895 --> 12:10.688
No matter what happens,

12:12.315 --> 12:14.233
I will remember you.

12:59.445 --> 13:01.698
I can't go further
because the road is blocked.

13:01.781 --> 13:04.492
You can't go further? Here, take it.

13:07.120 --> 13:09.914
Why is the road blocked?

13:09.998 --> 13:11.165
For goodness' sake.

13:11.416 --> 13:13.459
-For goodness' sake.
-The hour is late,

13:13.876 --> 13:16.629
so I didn't expect to see you.

13:16.713 --> 13:18.840
-Have you been well?
-Sure.

13:18.923 --> 13:23.594
I'm glad you're here. There are
many questions I've wanted to ask you.

13:23.678 --> 13:26.556
-Pardon?
-The house was ready quite a while ago,

13:26.639 --> 13:30.143
but why are the newlyweds
nowhere to be seen?

13:30.643 --> 13:32.854
As you know,

13:32.937 --> 13:37.942
Jeong Hyeok has an emergency
at the outpost line.

13:38.985 --> 13:40.194
Right?

13:40.445 --> 13:41.571
It's just that

13:42.155 --> 13:47.493
I saw a strange man go into the house.

13:47.994 --> 13:51.706
As the people's president
of this neighborhood,

13:51.789 --> 13:55.585
I was thinking
that maybe I should make a visit.

13:56.294 --> 14:00.048
I should have given this to you earlier.
Happy New Year.

14:00.131 --> 14:02.341
-You shouldn't have.
-You shouldn't have.

14:02.425 --> 14:06.179
That strange man you saw is my nephew.

14:06.262 --> 14:07.430
His name is Alberto.

14:09.348 --> 14:10.725
Alber...

14:10.808 --> 14:14.687
He recently came back from Europe
when he received the country's calling.

14:15.104 --> 14:16.898
I told him to stay in Pyongyang,

14:16.981 --> 14:20.651
but he insisted upon staying here
because he missed the countryside.

14:20.735 --> 14:22.612
-I see.
-Yes.

14:22.695 --> 14:24.655
The air quality is better here.

14:24.739 --> 14:25.698
Yes.

14:25.782 --> 14:26.699
Then...

14:30.203 --> 14:31.412
She seems to be in a hurry.

14:32.246 --> 14:34.165
She seems to be in a great hurry.

14:35.166 --> 14:37.752
I think she was lying
when she said he is her nephew.

14:38.503 --> 14:39.587
I agree.

14:40.129 --> 14:41.130
Is Dan having an affair?

14:43.508 --> 14:45.259
It will be a bloodbath.

14:58.815 --> 14:59.857
Hello.

14:59.941 --> 15:02.610
-Comrade Al.
-That's right. I am Comrade Al.

15:02.693 --> 15:05.321
We have met before, Mother.

15:06.322 --> 15:08.157
-Mother?
-I was thinking

15:08.241 --> 15:11.536
about visiting you in Pyongyang.

15:11.619 --> 15:13.287
-Me?
-Of course.

15:13.371 --> 15:17.500
I am honored that
you've come all the way here in person.

15:18.126 --> 15:20.086
-Dan is here, right?
-Yes.

15:20.837 --> 15:22.004
She is here,

15:22.713 --> 15:24.924
but she drank vodka until sunrise
and passed out.

15:25.007 --> 15:26.300
Again?

15:27.802 --> 15:29.804
I was about to wake her up

15:30.805 --> 15:33.099
and make her eat some pollack soup.

15:33.182 --> 15:34.183
Is that so?

15:36.978 --> 15:37.812
Could it be that

15:38.896 --> 15:42.733
Dan slept here without telling you?

15:42.984 --> 15:46.904
Her cell phone was off all day.

15:46.988 --> 15:50.616
Gosh, you must have been startled.

15:51.409 --> 15:54.370
I was a bit startled, but...

15:57.081 --> 15:59.000
I will apologize to you in her stead,

15:59.083 --> 16:02.336
so please don't scold Dan too much.

16:06.007 --> 16:09.093
-Where in the world is Dan?
-She is in this room.

16:09.177 --> 16:10.219
-This room?
-Yes.

16:12.263 --> 16:15.725
For goodness' sake. I can't believe her.

16:15.808 --> 16:18.769
Wake up right this instant!

16:23.483 --> 16:25.985
What do you think you are doing?

16:32.492 --> 16:34.911
Mother, you haven't had dinner yet, right?

16:35.203 --> 16:37.246
Please come on out and eat.

16:42.543 --> 16:45.922
All of these side dishes look familiar.

16:46.506 --> 16:50.468
I think they were in my fridge
until yesterday.

16:55.473 --> 16:57.934
Every table needs candlelight.

17:00.603 --> 17:04.106
I heard that you are a British citizen.

17:04.774 --> 17:06.275
What do your parents do?

17:07.109 --> 17:09.028
-Mom.
-My father used to run a business.

17:09.612 --> 17:11.155
He passed away a long time ago, though.

17:11.239 --> 17:13.282
My mother remarried,

17:13.991 --> 17:16.911
and I haven't seen her in 17 years.

17:17.578 --> 17:18.871
Is that so?

17:20.831 --> 17:26.295
What kind of relationship
do you have with Dan?

17:26.379 --> 17:30.883
I have a crush on Dan.

17:32.718 --> 17:36.013
I know that she likes

17:36.097 --> 17:38.474
and is engaged to another man.

17:39.892 --> 17:40.977
Why do you like

17:42.019 --> 17:43.062
Dan?

17:43.813 --> 17:46.482
Her disciplined sternness

17:47.525 --> 17:50.236
and noble elegance that comes from it.

17:52.154 --> 17:55.366
Her confidence and grace
which make her strong before anyone.

17:55.950 --> 17:57.368
All of those are the reasons.

17:58.244 --> 18:02.456
I think they were passed down
from her mother's side.

18:05.251 --> 18:06.460
I like him.

18:07.044 --> 18:10.923
He figured out
that your elegance comes from me.

18:11.549 --> 18:13.217
He is a wise man

18:14.969 --> 18:16.637
who has an eye for people.

18:17.597 --> 18:19.849
We don't have that kind of relationship.

18:20.516 --> 18:23.019
But he carried you home on his back,

18:23.102 --> 18:26.606
and you spent the night with him
at the apartment I got you.

18:26.689 --> 18:28.232
I told you, didn't I?

18:28.441 --> 18:31.110
I only let him stay over
because of some situation.

18:31.402 --> 18:34.822
Then when Jeong Hyeok returns
from the outpost line,

18:34.905 --> 18:38.200
-will you marry him as planned?
-Why wouldn't I?

18:38.701 --> 18:41.329
I am Jeong Hyeok's fiancÃ©e.

18:42.955 --> 18:44.957
JURI MOTEL

19:06.395 --> 19:07.730
It's you.

19:07.813 --> 19:10.816
-Who are you?
-I think you know.

19:11.692 --> 19:15.237
I remember. We talked on the phone,
Mr. Ri Jeong Hyeok.

19:23.329 --> 19:25.790
Instead of showing up to an appointment,
you sent someone else.

19:25.873 --> 19:29.460
I had an emergency that day.

19:29.543 --> 19:32.880
I shouldn't have done that.
I did you a disservice. I am sorry.

19:33.798 --> 19:35.257
Gu Seung-jun told me

19:35.549 --> 19:38.552
that you are a talented broker,
but I should never trust you.

19:38.636 --> 19:43.182
Given the nature of the job,
I connect people,

19:43.265 --> 19:45.309
but I'm not necessarily loyal to them.

19:48.145 --> 19:49.772
You don't need to be loyal to me.

19:50.439 --> 19:52.900
Just answer the questions I ask.

19:54.026 --> 19:55.611
I have a question.

19:56.237 --> 20:00.574
It seems like the Military World Games
will end in five days.

20:00.658 --> 20:03.911
Does the team's bus return that day?

20:04.495 --> 20:05.496
Yes.

20:05.579 --> 20:08.249
We need to get on that bus no matter what.

20:09.417 --> 20:10.459
I see.

20:12.211 --> 20:17.425
And it would be the safest for Jeong Hyeok
to take that bus.

20:18.801 --> 20:22.930
His father took measures
despite the danger.

20:24.640 --> 20:29.145
But if he doesn't go back then,
he won't be safe anymore.

20:30.479 --> 20:32.565
It won't do if he fails to go back.

20:33.399 --> 20:34.650
He must go back

20:35.901 --> 20:36.944
no matter what.

20:38.946 --> 20:40.740
She told you not to come?

20:40.823 --> 20:44.869
That's right. She said
she will do the housekeeping for now,

20:45.077 --> 20:47.538
so I haven't gone to her place
for two weeks.

20:47.621 --> 20:48.581
Are you saying

20:49.123 --> 20:51.500
Yoon Se-ri does the laundry
and cleans the house

20:52.126 --> 20:55.379
without a housemaid?

20:55.463 --> 20:57.298
AUTOMATIC

21:05.598 --> 21:07.892
Se-ri, what are you doing?

21:07.975 --> 21:09.226
I am cleaning.

21:10.352 --> 21:11.687
With that?

21:15.524 --> 21:18.569
There are so many interesting things
in South Korea.

21:19.987 --> 21:23.741
I would buy everything
if only you could take them back.

21:28.412 --> 21:31.499
This is like a magical pass.

21:32.750 --> 21:34.710
People usually call it M.C.

21:34.794 --> 21:37.296
-What's that?
-Mom's card.

21:37.880 --> 21:41.258
Since this is Se-ri's card,
let's call it S.C.

21:41.342 --> 21:43.385
Get to the point.
What do you want us to do with it?

21:43.469 --> 21:46.305
S.C. is a card with no spending limit.

21:46.680 --> 21:49.058
You can buy anything you want with it.

21:49.141 --> 21:50.351
Really?

21:50.851 --> 21:51.936
You have no fear.

21:52.520 --> 21:55.105
Don't you believe me when I tell you
that I will make you a beggar

21:55.189 --> 21:57.107
-in your later years?
-No.

21:57.191 --> 21:59.652
Go ahead and spend all of my fortunes.

21:59.735 --> 22:01.904
Do something about your clothes.

22:03.489 --> 22:04.824
Pyo Chi Su, you are the worst.

22:05.658 --> 22:07.576
This is driving me crazy.

22:07.785 --> 22:09.745
You guys are like fashion terrorists.

22:10.329 --> 22:12.581
Terrorists? Who do you think we are?

22:12.665 --> 22:16.126
-We aren't terrorists.
-We aren't like that.

22:19.672 --> 22:23.133
Fashion terrorists have nothing to do
with an actual terror attack.

22:23.217 --> 22:26.095
It means that you have
no sense of fashion.

22:26.762 --> 22:27.763
Really?

22:29.265 --> 22:31.475
We do have a sense of fashion!

22:31.559 --> 22:34.645
No, you don't. So do your best.

22:34.728 --> 22:38.107
Before you leave,

22:38.691 --> 22:41.277
I want to give you a present.

22:41.443 --> 22:45.030
Buy everything you've wanted to get, eat,

22:45.614 --> 22:48.117
and wear so far.

22:48.951 --> 22:50.077
Make sure you do that.

22:56.750 --> 22:57.793
Chi Su.

22:59.545 --> 23:03.173
Upon a glimpse, South Korea seems to be
a wealthy country.

23:03.257 --> 23:06.218
But the marketplace reveals the truth.

23:07.177 --> 23:10.681
Look at these pants.
They are ripped up like a rag.

23:12.057 --> 23:15.644
They should have patched them up
before selling them.

23:15.728 --> 23:18.230
I think people wear such jeans for style.

23:18.314 --> 23:21.984
Style, my foot! Your knees will get cold.

23:23.485 --> 23:24.612
My goodness.

23:36.624 --> 23:38.334
Give me the same pair of jeans.

23:44.214 --> 23:45.466
Do you like it?

23:46.300 --> 23:47.301
Buy it in every color.

23:48.260 --> 23:49.428
Buy ten of it.

23:49.678 --> 23:50.846
Can I really do that?

23:51.722 --> 23:53.932
My siblings will love it.

23:54.016 --> 23:55.184
Of course.

23:55.517 --> 23:57.686
One costs...

23:58.729 --> 23:59.897
Five thousand won?

24:00.773 --> 24:02.066
It's not cheap, but...

24:02.149 --> 24:03.817
Forget it. Buy everything.

24:03.901 --> 24:06.195
Are there clothes you like?

24:06.278 --> 24:10.074
There are so many clothes
that I don't know what to pick.

24:10.324 --> 24:11.450
This is...

24:14.995 --> 24:16.497
the only thing I need.

24:18.040 --> 24:19.917
-How does it move?
-My goodness.

24:20.000 --> 24:22.628
You know

24:23.170 --> 24:27.591
Tonight

24:27.675 --> 24:31.136
I am the same as always

24:32.137 --> 24:33.430
Thoughts of you

24:33.555 --> 24:35.099
What are they doing?

24:36.433 --> 24:37.685
I think they are beggars.

24:38.394 --> 24:39.937
I knew it.

24:40.562 --> 24:42.481
There are beggars everywhere.

24:43.774 --> 24:46.235
I want those clothes.

24:49.863 --> 24:51.532
In secret

25:09.383 --> 25:10.426
Hey.

25:16.223 --> 25:18.892
Let's talk about changing
the chairwoman of Se-ri's Choice

25:18.976 --> 25:20.602
once more.

25:20.686 --> 25:24.565
That item was rejected
after Chairwoman Yoon came back.

25:25.065 --> 25:26.150
What if

25:26.734 --> 25:30.028
Chairwoman Yoon has major faults

25:30.112 --> 25:33.532
that keep her from running the company?

25:35.826 --> 25:39.413
Don't you want to know
where Chairwoman Yoon was

25:39.496 --> 25:40.873
while she was missing?

25:49.631 --> 25:52.760
You want to backstab her
as soon as she comes back alive.

25:52.843 --> 25:55.220
You are one impressive woman.

25:55.804 --> 25:59.516
I am working hard
to make your son successful.

26:00.100 --> 26:03.437
If you make me a bitch,
I will be disappointed.

26:04.605 --> 26:07.733
No mother would sacrifice her daughter
to make her son successful.

26:09.860 --> 26:11.987
I know where Se-ri has been,

26:12.070 --> 26:15.115
and the fact that you and Se-hyeong
stopped her from escaping sooner.

26:15.699 --> 26:18.243
My husband knows as well.

26:19.244 --> 26:21.330
Se-hyeong is in Hong Kong for work, right?

26:21.497 --> 26:24.249
Tell him to come back right away.
Come to the house with him.

26:29.880 --> 26:32.841
Last night, Cha Sang-u posted something

26:32.925 --> 26:35.844
that was clearly meant for you
on his social media account.

26:39.306 --> 26:40.265
Look at this.

26:43.435 --> 26:44.853
It must be about another woman.

26:44.937 --> 26:47.564
"I am glad you are back safely.
Shall we go out again?

26:47.648 --> 26:50.317
It's 2 a.m.
and alcohol is making me honest."

26:50.901 --> 26:53.862
It's clearly and definitely a message
for you.

26:54.988 --> 26:57.658
Why are you making a fuss
about a drunk man's words?

26:57.825 --> 26:58.867
Stop and...

26:58.951 --> 27:02.579
But reporters keep asking us
if he and you will get back together.

27:02.663 --> 27:03.997
Get back together, my foot!

27:04.581 --> 27:06.124
It has happened before.

27:06.208 --> 27:08.210
Was it when she dated Shin Yeong-woong?

27:08.293 --> 27:10.629
No, it was when she dated
that idol singer, Won Ji-hun.

27:10.712 --> 27:12.381
They dated on and off.

27:12.464 --> 27:14.758
-It was a total mess.
-Seriously.

27:14.842 --> 27:15.884
Stop!

27:16.552 --> 27:18.637
I have so much work

27:18.720 --> 27:20.806
and absolutely no time
for this useless babbling.

27:21.807 --> 27:23.267
Hurry up and get back to your work.

27:24.977 --> 27:25.936
Yes, ma'am.

27:29.731 --> 27:31.108
Lee Hyeok, what are you doing?

27:31.608 --> 27:32.734
Come on.

27:32.818 --> 27:35.112
No. Hyeok stays.

27:35.696 --> 27:36.905
-What?
-I have

27:36.989 --> 27:40.200
important and secret orders for him.

27:40.868 --> 27:42.870
-Hurry up and get out.
-Okay.

28:02.264 --> 28:05.183
I guess you weren't lying when you said
you'd go back and date men.

28:08.186 --> 28:11.940
Those men just passed
through my life briefly.

28:13.525 --> 28:14.443
Is that so?

28:15.485 --> 28:17.905
Yes, it is.

28:20.824 --> 28:23.035
Am I passing through your life?

28:23.619 --> 28:25.454
Tell me if it happened already.

28:30.334 --> 28:31.501
My goodness.

28:31.627 --> 28:34.421
Little Hyeoky, are you jealous?

28:35.047 --> 28:36.173
No!

28:36.590 --> 28:38.091
Whose fault do you think it is?

28:38.884 --> 28:40.135
Are you saying it's my fault?

28:40.218 --> 28:42.596
You should have shown up sooner
in my life.

28:43.013 --> 28:45.557
How was I supposed to do that
with the ceasefire line between us?

28:45.641 --> 28:48.227
That's why I am so understanding.

28:48.310 --> 28:51.688
It's a sad history,
not your personal fault.

28:51.772 --> 28:53.523
In any case, it was hard for me too.

28:53.857 --> 28:56.068
"Is he the one?" Then he wasn't the one.

28:56.151 --> 28:59.112
"Is he the one?"
Then he wasn't the one either.

28:59.655 --> 29:02.950
Since my fated one was in North Korea,
I kept breaking up with men.

29:03.825 --> 29:06.828
It was so exhausting and stressful.

29:07.579 --> 29:11.124
Since we met each other
after many twists and turns,

29:11.833 --> 29:13.627
why don't we bunk off?

29:16.004 --> 29:17.214
Are you up for it?

30:21.737 --> 30:24.489
Are you satisfied
that you bunked off today?

30:26.158 --> 30:29.036
The day you spend after bunking off
is never satisfactory.

30:29.119 --> 30:31.204
Since it always happens without a plan,

30:31.288 --> 30:33.540
you can't do much despite the will.

30:34.124 --> 30:36.585
But it's memorable

30:37.085 --> 30:38.420
even if you don't do much.

30:39.463 --> 30:41.340
Have you ever bunked off before?

30:42.632 --> 30:44.301
-Yes.
-What did you do?

30:45.761 --> 30:47.387
I didn't do much too.

30:48.597 --> 30:51.850
I skipped my class
and went outside to take photos.

30:53.602 --> 30:57.230
Then I saw someone
who was thinking about jumping off

30:57.314 --> 30:59.733
a tall bridge.

31:00.817 --> 31:01.985
Who?

31:03.111 --> 31:05.697
She was a woman. She was my type.

31:10.494 --> 31:13.538
I see why you said
such days are memorable.

31:15.290 --> 31:17.918
I asked her to take a picture of me.

31:18.001 --> 31:21.296
Stop it. You don't need to give me
the details.

31:21.922 --> 31:24.466
She asked me if she must take it
at such a scary place.

31:27.094 --> 31:29.846
With trembling hands, she took the camera.

31:44.903 --> 31:46.363
Where is that?

31:48.156 --> 31:49.199
Switzerland.

31:50.742 --> 31:52.536
On Panorama Bridge Sigriswil.

31:56.665 --> 31:58.917
That woman was quite memorable.

31:59.000 --> 32:01.044
Even after that, I wondered

32:01.878 --> 32:03.797
if she was doing all right

32:05.549 --> 32:07.050
and if she would do anything bad

32:08.343 --> 32:09.302
every now and then.

32:11.972 --> 32:13.682
Because she was my type.

32:31.867 --> 32:32.826
Then...

32:34.703 --> 32:36.663
the woman next to you was

32:37.831 --> 32:38.832
Ms. Seo Dan?

32:40.959 --> 32:43.587
You said I could do better than her.

32:45.422 --> 32:47.007
I wonder...

32:48.675 --> 32:50.385
how many times we have met.

32:56.266 --> 32:57.434
I am

32:59.269 --> 33:00.729
very happy now.

33:03.565 --> 33:05.233
They say

33:06.193 --> 33:09.654
one sees the flashback
of the best moments in their life

33:10.697 --> 33:12.282
for a moment

33:13.116 --> 33:16.786
before they die.

33:19.414 --> 33:21.208
I think this will be

33:23.210 --> 33:24.961
one of those moments.

33:53.114 --> 33:54.282
We should win, right?

33:54.366 --> 33:56.076
-What the...
-Look at him.

33:56.493 --> 33:59.454
-Oh, come on!
-What was that?

34:00.038 --> 34:02.916
-What are you doing?
-Hey!

34:02.999 --> 34:04.584
What's with all the fuss?

34:04.668 --> 34:06.586
They're watching a soccer game.

34:07.796 --> 34:09.839
What an ultimate entertainment.

34:10.340 --> 34:12.008
It's an international competition.

34:12.092 --> 34:14.469
Hey, who cares
about international competitions?

34:15.053 --> 34:17.472
-Chi Su is right.
-Right.

34:17.556 --> 34:20.267
We must focus on our mission,
which is to send Captain Ri

34:20.350 --> 34:22.227
safely back home, and go back home.

34:22.310 --> 34:24.771
-But it's a match between Korea and Japan.
-What?

34:25.605 --> 34:27.274
JAPAN: 0, KOREA: 0

34:27.357 --> 34:28.650
Go, go!

34:28.733 --> 34:31.194
-Keep going!
-Just go!

34:32.487 --> 34:34.531
-Run!
-Run!

34:34.614 --> 34:36.741
-Run!
-Run faster!

34:36.825 --> 34:38.410
-Go!
-Shoot!

34:46.167 --> 34:47.460
Captain Ri!

34:47.544 --> 34:49.379
Se-ri!

34:57.053 --> 34:59.055
-Korea for the win!
-Korea for the win!

34:59.139 --> 35:02.142
-Republic of Korea!
-Republic of Korea!

35:03.768 --> 35:05.478
-Republic of Korea!
-Republic of Korea!

35:07.063 --> 35:08.732
-Republic of Korea!
-Republic of Korea!

35:10.525 --> 35:12.611
-There you go.
-Go!

35:15.864 --> 35:18.867
-Oh, come on!
-It was so close!

35:19.451 --> 35:21.828
-Good. Keep going.
-Go, go!

35:21.911 --> 35:23.622
-Go!
-Keep running!

35:23.705 --> 35:25.915
-Go!
-Shoot!

35:34.799 --> 35:35.967
-Cheers.
-Let's drink.

35:37.135 --> 35:38.219
That was great.

35:38.720 --> 35:41.848
I'm paying for all the chickens today.

35:56.780 --> 35:57.614
Yangsongi beoseot.

36:03.244 --> 36:05.580
Why do you always say words
that end with seot?

36:06.081 --> 36:07.040
Damn it.

36:07.123 --> 36:09.250
Drink it up.

36:09.334 --> 36:10.669
Drink up.

36:11.002 --> 36:13.171
-Hurry and drink up
-Hurry and drink up

36:13.254 --> 36:15.674
-Drink it up now
-Drink it up now

36:15.757 --> 36:18.301
If you don't, you're a coward
If you drink it, you are a hero

36:18.385 --> 36:19.302
One more time!

36:19.386 --> 36:21.429
-Hurry and drink up
-Hurry and drink up

36:21.513 --> 36:23.556
-Drink it up now
-Drink it up now

36:23.640 --> 36:26.726
If you don't, you're a coward
If you drink it, you are a hero

36:37.821 --> 36:38.697
Thank you...

36:44.411 --> 36:46.955
It's even nicer to see you out here.

36:48.707 --> 36:53.253
When I found out that you betrayed me,
I got angry at first.

36:54.379 --> 36:56.297
But I understood.

36:57.340 --> 37:01.761
One can't only live off
the same food all the time.

37:04.264 --> 37:08.184
However, you must face the reality.

37:09.936 --> 37:11.646
Do you think

37:11.730 --> 37:15.108
the Director of the GPB will protect you
when you get back?

37:15.859 --> 37:20.655
After all, you're the person
who killed his eldest son.

37:23.825 --> 37:26.953
After being used, you will be abandoned.

37:30.039 --> 37:34.169
Was it the Director of the GPB
that has been providing for your family?

37:34.252 --> 37:39.674
Was it Ri Jeong Hyeok who freed
your old mother from the prison?

37:41.342 --> 37:43.845
Could you please just
turn a blind eye to me?

37:45.555 --> 37:47.515
I would like to pay for what I did

37:48.641 --> 37:50.351
to Ri Mu Hyeok.

37:55.815 --> 37:59.527
Paying your debt to a dead man or...

38:00.528 --> 38:02.781
saving your only child's life.
What's your choice?

38:03.948 --> 38:05.116
What do you mean?

38:09.245 --> 38:11.206
It's U Pil from this morning.

38:13.166 --> 38:15.168
Sir.

38:15.251 --> 38:19.464
Loyalty and Justice.
They're all good. But,

38:20.048 --> 38:23.593
the reason I don't pursue them is
not because I don't know they're good.

38:24.469 --> 38:26.095
Rather than those fancy ideas,

38:26.179 --> 38:30.934
I choose to protect my family and my kids.
That's why.

38:31.017 --> 38:34.187
Who can blame that?

38:37.899 --> 38:41.653
And I used to be a child beggar
who was born on the street.

38:42.612 --> 38:46.950
I have no one to protect
and nothing to fear.

38:47.450 --> 38:50.787
That's why I can risk everything
and just go for it.

38:50.870 --> 38:54.666
If I catch Ri Jeong Hyeok here
and take Yoon Se-ri back home,

38:54.749 --> 38:59.420
I can go up to a higher position.

39:04.008 --> 39:04.884
So...

39:06.302 --> 39:07.762
make your decision.

39:08.388 --> 39:09.514
Comrade.

39:22.819 --> 39:25.238
I think it's better
that you sleep up here.

39:25.321 --> 39:27.574
I said I'm fine. Enjoy your bed.

39:28.575 --> 39:29.826
Thank you, Sir.

39:32.161 --> 39:34.539
Before you guys met us,
you slept in a sauna?

39:35.206 --> 39:36.249
Yes.

39:36.916 --> 39:39.377
But that place was really great too.

39:39.711 --> 39:42.797
There are so many interesting things
in South Korea.

39:44.674 --> 39:45.842
What else was interesting?

39:46.968 --> 39:50.138
I went to a place called internet cafe
with Ju Meok.

39:50.221 --> 39:52.849
I did this thing called computer game
for the first time.

39:53.474 --> 39:55.268
You played a computer game too.

39:56.644 --> 39:59.272
Well, it's a good experience to have
at your age.

40:00.607 --> 40:01.983
At first,

40:02.233 --> 40:05.653
I saw the amateurs shooting rifles
like children.

40:06.237 --> 40:09.198
So I thought, "I will show them
how to do it," and started to play.

40:11.743 --> 40:14.412
But it was harder than I'd thought.

40:15.997 --> 40:17.707
It's not as easy as it looks.

40:18.207 --> 40:19.751
That's right.

40:20.668 --> 40:25.673
So I studied the features
of the weapons and armors I had.

40:27.008 --> 40:29.344
But then some South Korean punk

40:29.427 --> 40:32.263
armed with expensive gears showed up
and messed up everything.

40:32.347 --> 40:33.848
Oh, no.

40:33.932 --> 40:37.268
I got angry and said,
"Stop hiding behind the computer.

40:37.352 --> 40:39.479
Let me see you face."

40:40.396 --> 40:42.440
-And?
-He didn't show up.

40:43.024 --> 40:48.029
After all, he was one of those typical
rich and cowardly capitalist bluffers.

40:48.988 --> 40:50.198
That stupid Tomato Cultivator.

40:52.492 --> 40:54.953
What was your name in the game?

40:55.536 --> 40:58.206
It was Desperate Effort.

41:01.918 --> 41:04.963
-I see.
-So I--

41:05.046 --> 41:08.132
Why don't you stop talking
and go to bed now? It's late.

41:11.636 --> 41:12.720
Where are you going?

41:14.013 --> 41:15.223
To get some water.

41:17.558 --> 41:18.643
Sleep tight.

41:27.694 --> 41:28.778
What's wrong?

41:29.612 --> 41:30.822
If you're hungry...

41:33.992 --> 41:35.076
No, I'm not.

41:39.122 --> 41:41.416
Is it because you miss your family?

41:45.253 --> 41:47.255
You will soon be able to see them again.

41:48.881 --> 41:50.717
This is all because of me. I'm sorry.

42:01.853 --> 42:02.854
IGNORANCE IS DARKNESS!

42:02.937 --> 42:05.732
We have been thinking

42:05.815 --> 42:08.943
if there is any way
we could help you, Yeong Ae.

42:09.527 --> 42:13.781
And Myeong Sun
has something to say to you.

42:14.490 --> 42:16.284
-What is it?
-I can't reach my husband

42:16.367 --> 42:18.244
who went on a long-term business trip.

42:19.120 --> 42:20.913
So I went to his close friends

42:20.997 --> 42:22.707
and asked them some questions.

42:22.790 --> 42:26.502
Friends, you mean by the wiretappers?

42:26.586 --> 42:27.754
Yes.

42:27.879 --> 42:29.255
You know how good wiretappers are.

42:29.338 --> 42:31.632
There's nothing they don't know
about our village.

42:32.633 --> 42:33.801
You're right.

42:33.885 --> 42:34.844
Yes.

42:34.969 --> 42:37.513
Then what did his friends

42:37.597 --> 42:39.223
say to you?

42:39.307 --> 42:42.018
They said the incident
the Senior Colonel was involved

42:42.101 --> 42:43.811
happened because

42:44.979 --> 42:46.355
Lieutenant Commander Cho Cheol Gang

42:46.439 --> 42:48.816
tried to dig up dirt
on the Director of the GPB.

42:50.651 --> 42:53.154
-Oh, my. Yeong Ae.
-Goodness.

42:53.237 --> 42:56.240
How dare he tried to mess up
with such a high-ranking official.

42:56.324 --> 43:00.161
Cho Cheol Gang must have been
killed secretly.

43:00.244 --> 43:01.579
My goodness.

43:01.662 --> 43:04.791
Why does Ri Jeong Hyeok happen to be

43:04.874 --> 43:06.918
at the frontline now of all times?

43:07.627 --> 43:08.628
I know!

43:10.046 --> 43:11.589
It might not be the direct way

43:11.672 --> 43:13.424
to the Director of the GPB,

43:13.508 --> 43:16.594
I know a detour nearby.

43:17.345 --> 43:19.555
-What?
-The Director of the GPB's

43:20.640 --> 43:23.434
-future daughter-in-law's mother's...
-Yes?

43:23.518 --> 43:25.394
nephew who used to live in Europe.

43:26.729 --> 43:27.563
What?

43:27.647 --> 43:31.400
Goodness. I can't believe I took a bath
with the water boiled in a cauldron.

43:33.277 --> 43:35.488
Now I have done everything.

43:36.531 --> 43:38.908
Comrade Nephew from Europe,
are you in there?

43:38.991 --> 43:40.785
Please open the door.

43:40.952 --> 43:42.036
Maybe he's not in there.

43:42.120 --> 43:43.287
Yes, he is.

43:43.371 --> 43:44.914
He's in there.

43:44.997 --> 43:48.167
We just saw the cauldron's steam

43:48.251 --> 43:51.170
coming out of this apartment.

43:51.254 --> 43:52.588
There was steam indeed.

43:52.672 --> 43:53.923
Right?

43:54.006 --> 43:55.258
Keep knocking.

43:56.425 --> 43:57.969
Open the door.

43:58.052 --> 43:59.887
We can unlock the door if we want.

44:00.471 --> 44:02.306
But that's illegal.

44:02.473 --> 44:04.559
-What's up?
-It's Dan.

44:04.642 --> 44:07.812
Well, as the President of the village,
I just wanted to check--

44:07.895 --> 44:08.771
Please come in.

44:08.855 --> 44:10.022
-"Come in"?
-Okay.

44:15.528 --> 44:16.779
Oh, my goodness.

44:19.991 --> 44:20.867
Hey.

44:23.035 --> 44:24.078
Hello.

44:24.704 --> 44:26.747
Looks like I have many visitors.

44:36.132 --> 44:40.553
Oh, my. I'm sorry
that we all suddenly have showed up.

44:40.636 --> 44:42.555
Hopefully we didn't
make you feel uncomfortable.

44:42.638 --> 44:43.806
I feel uncomfortable.

44:46.559 --> 44:49.103
Yeong Ae, isn't it great?

44:49.187 --> 44:54.025
We came to meet the Director of the GPB's
daughter-in-law's mother's

44:54.567 --> 44:57.904
nephew who used to live in Europe.

44:57.987 --> 45:01.574
But we happened to meet
his future daughter-in-law.

45:01.657 --> 45:02.992
What's your business?

45:09.957 --> 45:10.917
This is

45:11.500 --> 45:14.086
what I got from my mother-in-law.

45:14.921 --> 45:17.715
I have been treasuring it dearly.

45:17.798 --> 45:19.425
Then keep treasuring it dearly.

45:22.470 --> 45:25.014
As a matter of fact,

45:25.514 --> 45:28.309
my husband is imprisoned
by the State Security Department.

45:28.935 --> 45:32.813
Could you put in a word for him
to the Director of the GPB,

45:33.147 --> 45:34.398
who will be your father-in-law?

45:34.482 --> 45:36.359
I don't accept personal requests.

45:37.318 --> 45:39.070
Is there anything else you want to say?

45:39.654 --> 45:43.574
Come on, Dan.

45:43.658 --> 45:46.494
Don't be so uptight.

45:47.954 --> 45:51.791
She might sound cold
as the cold wind in the winter,

45:51.874 --> 45:53.626
but her heart is warm
like a spring breeze.

45:53.709 --> 45:56.712
Please leave the name of your husband.

45:56.879 --> 45:59.966
I will put in a good word for him
with my aunt.

46:00.049 --> 46:02.927
Oh, my. Comrade Nephew from Europe

46:03.010 --> 46:05.012
can talk sense, right?

46:05.096 --> 46:08.724
Please take good care of it.

46:08.808 --> 46:10.726
Don't you worry.

46:10.810 --> 46:13.729
By the way, I feel like
I have seen you before.

46:14.313 --> 46:15.564
Me?

46:16.273 --> 46:19.902
I saw you coming out
of Captain Ri's house the other day.

46:19.986 --> 46:21.278
-Is that true?
-Yes.

46:22.405 --> 46:23.739
I sent him on an errand.

46:23.823 --> 46:25.324
I needed to pick up something.

46:25.408 --> 46:27.827
-I see.
-I see.

46:30.329 --> 46:31.163
That's right.

46:34.166 --> 46:36.460
Goodness. I'm finally outside.
It's all thanks to you.

46:36.544 --> 46:39.380
I have been staying home
these last few days and it was hard.

46:42.216 --> 46:43.551
Tell me.

46:43.634 --> 46:45.469
Why did you go to Jeong Hyeok's place?

46:46.053 --> 46:48.014
You know Jeong Hyeok is at the frontline.

46:49.390 --> 46:51.267
Don't you think of lying to me.

46:54.228 --> 46:57.440
I don't lie to you, Dan. I decided not to.

47:00.026 --> 47:01.277
The thing is...

47:02.319 --> 47:04.905
Ri Jeong Hyeok contacted me
from the frontline.

47:05.781 --> 47:06.699
Why?

47:08.200 --> 47:10.870
Cho Cheol Gang didn't die
while being transported.

47:11.996 --> 47:13.122
He disappeared.

47:13.205 --> 47:15.583
He went to South Korea.
He wants to bring Se-ri back

47:15.666 --> 47:18.169
and destroy Ri Jeong Hyeok's family.

47:18.836 --> 47:19.712
And?

47:21.672 --> 47:23.090
So Ri Jeong Hyeok...

47:25.217 --> 47:26.260
went to Seoul.

47:28.637 --> 47:31.223
To save Se-ri and catch Cho Cheol Gang.

47:33.809 --> 47:36.395
He didn't want to trouble
people around him,

47:36.479 --> 47:39.857
so he didn't tell anyone about it
and asked me favors.

47:39.940 --> 47:43.486
So I ran some errands
and set him up with some people.

47:43.569 --> 47:45.654
I'm not sure why I did that, but...

47:48.949 --> 47:49.992
Dan.

47:51.077 --> 47:52.203
Are you okay?

47:52.828 --> 47:56.582
Dan. I'm sorry.

47:57.083 --> 47:58.709
Don't cry--

48:10.554 --> 48:12.640
All right. Tell me what you found out.

48:13.474 --> 48:14.642
Myeong Eun.

48:14.934 --> 48:18.395
There is good news and bad news.

48:19.105 --> 48:20.439
What would you like to hear first?

48:20.523 --> 48:24.527
No funny business, you punk.
Just tell me already.

48:25.027 --> 48:27.738
First, Alberto Gu

48:27.905 --> 48:30.449
is indeed a businessman from the UK.

48:32.118 --> 48:34.495
He owns international businesses

48:34.578 --> 48:36.539
all over the world.

48:37.164 --> 48:39.625
-What's the bad news?
-This is the bad news.

48:40.209 --> 48:41.460
What are you saying?

48:41.544 --> 48:45.214
The Director of the GPB recently
tracked down

48:45.381 --> 48:48.300
illegal businesses on a large scale.

48:48.509 --> 48:50.678
He tracked down smugglers, drug dealers,

48:50.761 --> 48:53.681
and those who got paid
for hiding criminals.

48:53.848 --> 48:54.807
Were you all right?

48:54.890 --> 48:57.059
Of course. Thanks to your wealth,

48:57.143 --> 49:00.312
I have never been interested in money.

49:00.771 --> 49:03.399
-And?
-There's a British business man

49:03.482 --> 49:05.109
who is involved in the incident.

49:05.192 --> 49:08.279
And that's Alberto Gu.

49:09.822 --> 49:11.198
What?

49:11.282 --> 49:13.409
The State Security Department
is looking for him.

49:13.492 --> 49:16.620
Apparently, he swindled
a lot of money in South Korea

49:16.704 --> 49:19.206
and escaped to our country.

49:23.586 --> 49:25.421
Then what's the good news?

49:25.504 --> 49:28.674
-Right. The good news is...
-Yes?

49:28.757 --> 49:32.094
Dan seems to know about this.

49:32.178 --> 49:34.513
-What?
-She knew it from the first place.

49:34.597 --> 49:36.223
It means

49:36.307 --> 49:39.685
Dan didn't fall for a swindler at least.

49:39.768 --> 49:41.604
You lunatic.

49:41.687 --> 49:43.814
How is that good news?

49:43.898 --> 49:46.233
What's wrong with you?

49:46.317 --> 49:48.485
What's wrong? Why do you always hit me?

49:48.569 --> 49:50.237
-What is it that I did wrong?
-You punk!

50:02.249 --> 50:03.250
What are you doing?

50:04.668 --> 50:09.381
I will send Ju Meok on an errand later,
and I want him to look pretty.

50:11.258 --> 50:12.468
Ju Meok, you can remove it now.

50:15.930 --> 50:16.972
What errand?

50:17.056 --> 50:20.059
He will look
like a very sophisticated South Korean

50:20.142 --> 50:21.977
and pick up something.

50:22.061 --> 50:25.481
I would make a sophisticated South Korean
very well.

50:26.190 --> 50:28.651
Yesterday, I was standing
at an intersection,

50:28.734 --> 50:31.028
and people asked me directions.

50:31.362 --> 50:33.197
They thought I was from Seoul.

50:34.406 --> 50:35.741
That's not it.

50:35.950 --> 50:38.202
Ju Meok, I think you should get changed

50:38.285 --> 50:39.745
before you go.

50:39.828 --> 50:41.163
What? I need to get changed?

50:41.247 --> 50:43.832
Yes. Here, we don't wear just anything

50:43.916 --> 50:46.377
when we run errands.

50:50.005 --> 50:51.548
-Oh, my.
-You look gorgeous.

50:51.632 --> 50:52.549
You look great.

50:52.633 --> 50:54.635
It suits you very well.

50:54.885 --> 50:56.095
-Does it?
-Yes.

50:56.178 --> 50:59.473
Do South Koreans really dress like that
when they run errands?

50:59.556 --> 51:01.141
Yes, we do. I told you.

52:32.107 --> 52:34.693
Se-ri usually doesn't ask me
favors like this,

52:34.985 --> 52:37.154
but she said she really would like me
to do this favor.

52:40.199 --> 52:43.744
She said you were one of the people

52:43.827 --> 52:45.371
she likes the most.

52:49.333 --> 52:53.045
She told me you came from
somewhere really far away to see me.

52:53.921 --> 52:55.506
Thank you.

52:58.175 --> 52:59.301
Not at all.

53:02.721 --> 53:06.016
If there's anything you'd like to say,
feel free to do so.

53:16.985 --> 53:19.029
You said

53:21.156 --> 53:22.658
those who love each other

53:23.617 --> 53:24.660
will always meet again.

53:33.001 --> 53:34.336
No matter...

53:37.589 --> 53:38.882
how far you are...

53:42.678 --> 53:46.306
You'll always come back to each other.

53:49.184 --> 53:51.186
Yes. That's right.

53:53.147 --> 53:54.606
True love will always return.

54:35.689 --> 54:38.400
-Where's Ju Meok?
-He said he's not hungry.

54:38.484 --> 54:40.110
Why not?

54:40.611 --> 54:45.324
He refuses to eat anything
on top of the sacred meal he had

54:45.407 --> 54:47.826
with Actress Choi Ji-woo.

54:52.664 --> 54:56.502
Ju Meok, let's meet again.

54:59.671 --> 55:01.048
Okay, Ji-woo.

55:01.673 --> 55:02.883
Let's meet again.

55:07.971 --> 55:10.849
But the only way to do that
is through unification.

55:15.270 --> 55:18.023
Did you do your errand well?

55:18.106 --> 55:20.651
-Se-ri, you totally duped me.
-Let me see.

55:21.193 --> 55:23.487
How did you deceive me so easily?

55:23.570 --> 55:25.614
Didn't you see me doing this

55:25.948 --> 55:26.907
earlier in the morning?

55:26.990 --> 55:28.742
Do South Koreans really dress like that

55:28.825 --> 55:30.202
when they run errands?

55:30.285 --> 55:31.995
Yes, we do. I told you.

55:32.287 --> 55:33.372
What is that?

55:35.457 --> 55:37.751
The American imperialism does this

55:37.834 --> 55:41.338
as a way of declaring that they will lie.

55:41.964 --> 55:45.592
That's right. So even though I did lie,

55:45.676 --> 55:47.469
God would've forgiven me.

55:50.389 --> 55:55.352
How are you so tolerant of yourself?

55:58.981 --> 56:01.149
Thank you so much.

56:01.817 --> 56:03.944
You made my lifetime dream come true.

56:05.654 --> 56:08.907
I'd have no regrets even if I died today.

56:09.324 --> 56:11.410
You got the award you deserved.

56:12.619 --> 56:14.663
Love for K-drama Award.

56:18.834 --> 56:21.253
Eun Dong, you received
the Hospitality Award.

56:27.968 --> 56:29.219
And...

56:31.638 --> 56:34.224
Chi Su, you received
the Fragrant Scalp Award.

56:41.481 --> 56:44.359
Are we saying our goodbyes once again?

56:46.987 --> 56:48.155
Yes.

56:50.824 --> 56:53.577
Why do we keep saying goodbye?

56:54.745 --> 56:57.664
Who knows? This may not be our last.

57:00.208 --> 57:05.213
Even still, we should say our goodbyes
in advance when we can.

57:10.344 --> 57:14.097
By the way, I gave you my card
so that you could splurge,

57:14.264 --> 57:16.016
but you didn't spend much.

57:16.767 --> 57:19.895
So I prepared a gift for each of you.

57:23.774 --> 57:25.776
Are you all ready to leave?

57:26.610 --> 57:28.028
-Yes, sir.
-Yes, sir.

57:28.111 --> 57:30.197
They'll be sending us another bus

57:31.323 --> 57:33.784
so that the other athletes won't notice.

57:36.453 --> 57:38.747
Aren't you coming with us?

57:42.042 --> 57:44.378
A man who goes by Manager Oh
will contact me.

57:45.837 --> 57:47.214
You can go first.

57:47.547 --> 57:49.549
I'll join you once I'm done.

57:55.263 --> 57:56.390
Good work.

57:57.432 --> 57:59.851
Now I'll lure Ri Jeong Hyeok

57:59.935 --> 58:02.354
through Manager Oh.

58:02.437 --> 58:05.023
In the meantime, act normally

58:05.524 --> 58:08.443
and report
Jeong Hyeok and Se-ri's whereabouts.

58:14.825 --> 58:16.159
Oh, my.

58:16.410 --> 58:18.453
I think something broke.

58:18.537 --> 58:20.956
That's understandable.

58:21.289 --> 58:22.624
Hold my hand, will you?

58:23.208 --> 58:25.168
All right.

58:32.134 --> 58:33.427
Father.

58:33.719 --> 58:35.971
Do you even know how old that is?

58:36.054 --> 58:38.015
You can't destroy them like this--

58:38.098 --> 58:39.766
What did you say?

58:39.850 --> 58:41.935
You should've told me the truth

58:42.019 --> 58:43.979
when you had the chance.

58:44.062 --> 58:45.105
Father!

58:46.106 --> 58:49.693
Are you going to believe these men
whom you've never met

58:50.569 --> 58:52.863
or me, your son?

58:55.449 --> 58:57.325
I trusted you.

58:57.409 --> 59:00.996
Then please keep doing so.

59:01.079 --> 59:03.498
-It's a misunderstanding.
-Shut up!

59:05.625 --> 59:09.004
Why do you think I appointed you
to that position?

59:09.087 --> 59:10.881
Because you're competent?

59:10.964 --> 59:12.340
Don't be ridiculous!

59:12.924 --> 59:14.634
It was because
you were the most incompetent.

59:15.719 --> 59:18.972
You're a doormat to your wife
and was conned so easily.

59:19.347 --> 59:21.933
I thought if you were aware
of how much you lacked,

59:22.017 --> 59:25.979
you'd ask others for help
instead of keeping everything to yourself.

59:26.063 --> 59:27.522
I thought you'd do that.

59:27.606 --> 59:29.691
That was why I gave you that position.

59:30.442 --> 59:33.070
Are you saying the reason
you picked me among my siblings

59:33.153 --> 59:35.906
was because I lacked the most?

59:35.989 --> 59:39.076
I was aware of that, but I had no idea
how much you had lacked!

59:41.161 --> 59:42.412
I made a mistake.

59:42.496 --> 59:44.956
I'm going to hold
a general meeting of stockholders soon.

59:45.832 --> 59:48.919
Just accept your fate
and get ready to be demoted.

59:50.045 --> 59:52.005
Why are you doing this?

59:56.343 --> 01:00:00.138
Father, I fully understand
why you're so upset.

01:00:00.972 --> 01:00:03.475
Please forgive us
for not telling you earlier.

01:00:04.059 --> 01:00:05.393
Get up.

01:00:06.061 --> 01:00:08.230
I don't want to see either one of you,
so get out!

01:00:11.399 --> 01:00:12.734
Please take a look at this.

01:00:13.068 --> 01:00:14.611
You can make your decision afterward.

01:00:18.990 --> 01:00:20.659
That's Gu Seung-jun.

01:00:20.742 --> 01:00:23.578
He and Se-ri were hiding together
up North.

01:00:25.747 --> 01:00:27.833
Do you really think it was coincidental?

01:00:32.129 --> 01:00:36.174
This is something we recently found out
while investigating.

01:00:37.008 --> 01:00:40.470
Do you remember Gu Myeong-su,
the president of Guryong Corporation,

01:00:40.637 --> 01:00:42.764
whose company you forcefully
took over 20 years ago?

01:00:43.265 --> 01:00:44.850
Seung-jun is his son.

01:00:45.559 --> 01:00:49.062
He had disguised himself
and approached our family on purpose.

01:00:49.146 --> 01:00:50.313
What?

01:00:50.397 --> 01:00:52.232
We had to confirm this

01:00:52.941 --> 01:00:54.734
before telling you.

01:00:55.402 --> 01:00:56.653
We apologize.

01:00:56.736 --> 01:00:59.030
Father, to be honest,

01:00:59.114 --> 01:01:01.408
all kinds of thoughts ran through my head.

01:01:01.491 --> 01:01:03.285
"Why were they spotted together
in North Korea

01:01:03.368 --> 01:01:04.953
when they had called off their marriage?

01:01:05.537 --> 01:01:09.749
Is the money he stole related to Se-ri?"

01:01:10.000 --> 01:01:12.669
But first, I told him
to send her back home.

01:01:12.752 --> 01:01:14.671
That's when he told me

01:01:14.754 --> 01:01:17.465
to give up half the money
that was scammed.

01:01:18.633 --> 01:01:19.718
But what could I do?

01:01:19.801 --> 01:01:22.387
My first priority was to bring Se-ri back.

01:01:24.139 --> 01:01:25.098
Is that so?

01:01:25.682 --> 01:01:28.518
I'll have to verify

01:01:28.602 --> 01:01:30.478
if you're still lying to me

01:01:30.562 --> 01:01:32.522
or if Se-ri really did that.

01:01:32.814 --> 01:01:36.234
If I find out that you lied once again,

01:01:36.902 --> 01:01:38.778
not only will you lose your position

01:01:38.862 --> 01:01:41.323
but everything that you currently have.

01:01:44.743 --> 01:01:45.994
Call her.

01:01:46.077 --> 01:01:47.996
I have nothing to say to you.

01:01:48.079 --> 01:01:50.582
I feel the same way.

01:01:51.249 --> 01:01:53.293
Father called for you,
so hurry up and come.

01:01:53.835 --> 01:01:55.462
Mom's not doing too well either.

01:01:56.963 --> 01:01:59.382
What's wrong? Is it because
of her low blood pressure?

01:01:59.466 --> 01:02:01.551
It's all because of you.

01:02:02.427 --> 01:02:05.180
Were you ever helpful to our family?

01:02:07.474 --> 01:02:09.226
Tell him I'll be on my way soon.

01:02:21.821 --> 01:02:23.406
The recording has ended.

01:02:29.204 --> 01:02:31.623
That's the route she takes to come here.

01:02:31.706 --> 01:02:33.833
She drives the car herself,

01:02:33.917 --> 01:02:35.418
so do as you wish.

01:02:36.002 --> 01:02:37.420
Does that mean

01:02:37.504 --> 01:02:40.423
you don't care whether I abduct

01:02:40.924 --> 01:02:42.509
or kill her?

01:02:44.177 --> 01:02:47.973
You can do whatever you want
to do with her.

01:02:49.015 --> 01:02:52.143
I just don't want her around me.

01:02:53.061 --> 01:02:55.105
That's all.

01:02:57.524 --> 01:03:00.110
Then I better get ready.

01:03:15.875 --> 01:03:17.210
Se-ri

01:03:18.211 --> 01:03:19.838
just left.

01:03:20.755 --> 01:03:22.799
We'll be leaving soon as well.

01:03:33.560 --> 01:03:34.644
NORTH KOREAN ATHLETICS TEAM

01:04:10.347 --> 01:04:14.392
NO ENTRY

01:05:37.600 --> 01:05:39.811
Jeong Hyeok should be here soon.

01:05:41.896 --> 01:05:44.858
Now that he'll arrive soon,

01:05:44.941 --> 01:05:47.777
I think I'm done with my job.
May I go now?

01:05:49.112 --> 01:05:50.613
Not yet.

01:05:51.197 --> 01:05:54.451
Once I kill him

01:05:54.534 --> 01:05:57.454
and get on the boat with Se-ri,

01:05:57.537 --> 01:05:59.998
that's when you'll be done with your job.

01:06:01.082 --> 01:06:03.751
I've arranged the time and place,

01:06:03.835 --> 01:06:06.838
and he'll arrive soon.
I think I'm done here.

01:06:20.477 --> 01:06:21.519
There he is.

01:06:47.170 --> 01:06:49.339
I knew it.

01:06:49.714 --> 01:06:51.799
I knew you'd come.

01:06:52.592 --> 01:06:54.552
You're not a coward

01:06:54.636 --> 01:06:58.598
who'd leave Se-ri behind and return
to the North, knowing I'm still here.

01:06:59.390 --> 01:07:00.433
You're right.

01:07:00.975 --> 01:07:04.354
I have no plans
to leave my woman here all alone. No.

01:07:04.854 --> 01:07:06.898
As long as a scumbag like you is here,

01:07:06.981 --> 01:07:09.275
I didn't plan on going back.

01:08:08.209 --> 01:08:09.377
Hey!

01:08:59.177 --> 01:09:00.386
Man Bok.

01:09:02.388 --> 01:09:04.015
Do you have something to tell me?

01:09:04.599 --> 01:09:06.351
If you do, please tell me.

01:09:13.691 --> 01:09:17.362
All my life, I've been reporting things
that I've eavesdropped on.

01:09:18.780 --> 01:09:20.531
But you're asking me to speak my mind.

01:09:23.117 --> 01:09:24.535
Thank you.

01:09:27.163 --> 01:09:28.122
I will

01:09:29.207 --> 01:09:30.917
tell you what's on my mind.

01:09:31.876 --> 01:09:33.878
I met with Cho Cheol Gang today.

01:09:34.712 --> 01:09:37.507
He threatened me with a photo of my child.

01:09:38.758 --> 01:09:40.343
I'm terrified.

01:09:41.886 --> 01:09:44.389
But I'm going to put up a fight this time.

01:09:44.472 --> 01:09:47.141
Aren't you coming with us?

01:09:51.062 --> 01:09:53.231
I need to stop by somewhere.

01:09:53.314 --> 01:09:55.650
A man who goes by Manager Oh
will contact me.

01:09:56.109 --> 01:09:57.652
You can go first.

01:09:57.735 --> 01:09:59.612
I'll join you once I'm done.

01:10:14.085 --> 01:10:15.753
Tell him I'll be on my way soon.

01:10:20.258 --> 01:10:22.135
I want to believe

01:10:24.053 --> 01:10:26.264
that my mom is sick
and everything my brother said.

01:10:26.347 --> 01:10:29.892
Do you truly believe that my brother
has colluded with Cho Cheol Gang

01:10:29.976 --> 01:10:31.686
and schemed this?

01:10:31.769 --> 01:10:33.229
We'll find out.

01:10:35.732 --> 01:10:38.735
Don't look so frightened. It's unlike you.

01:10:39.694 --> 01:10:41.487
What's there to be scared of
when we're here?

01:10:41.571 --> 01:10:42.822
-He's right.
-He's right.

01:10:51.205 --> 01:10:52.540
Se-ri

01:10:53.416 --> 01:10:55.042
just left.

01:11:46.969 --> 01:11:48.763
Eun Dong, how's it going?

01:11:48.846 --> 01:11:52.892
Don't overdo it
and make yourself stop growing!

01:11:53.893 --> 01:11:56.437
Don't worry. I'm doing fine.

01:12:03.778 --> 01:12:06.572
What was that? He's really one of a kind.

01:12:07.740 --> 01:12:09.742
Hey, be careful!

01:12:11.577 --> 01:12:12.954
Don't worry.

01:12:14.288 --> 01:12:15.998
We're from the special forces.

01:12:17.750 --> 01:12:20.753
It's cold out here. Wait inside for a bit.

01:12:21.546 --> 01:12:23.506
I hope they won't get hurt.

01:12:23.589 --> 01:12:25.842
Hey, don't move, okay?

01:12:25.925 --> 01:12:29.303
If you don't, I can hit you
every single time.

01:12:51.534 --> 01:12:52.869
Are you all right?

01:12:53.035 --> 01:12:54.912
-Yes.
-We're fine too.

01:12:55.246 --> 01:12:56.831
Man Bok.

01:12:57.832 --> 01:12:59.333
You startled me.

01:12:59.876 --> 01:13:02.461
All right. Let's go to the next place!

01:13:02.545 --> 01:13:03.671
-All right!
-All right!

01:13:11.012 --> 01:13:13.931
Hey, I'm serious! Be careful!

01:13:15.141 --> 01:13:18.227
Are you sure we won't have to pay
the monthly rent for the next year?

01:13:19.061 --> 01:13:21.314
You won't need to pay it for two years.

01:13:21.397 --> 01:13:22.815
So march forward!

01:13:24.901 --> 01:13:26.319
-Let's go!
-Okay!

01:14:02.605 --> 01:14:05.858
Captain Ri, we're here!

01:14:38.015 --> 01:14:40.768
I see that you've made a decision.

01:14:42.144 --> 01:14:43.854
So I'll make mine.

01:14:58.202 --> 01:14:59.745
Hey, hey, hey.

01:15:03.833 --> 01:15:05.960
Hey, what are you doing?

01:15:38.492 --> 01:15:39.785
Shoot.

01:15:40.786 --> 01:15:43.497
Why can't you kill
someone as trivial as him?

01:15:43.914 --> 01:15:45.124
You're so soft.

01:16:01.640 --> 01:16:03.017
What?

01:16:04.143 --> 01:16:05.686
What was that gunshot?

01:16:10.066 --> 01:16:11.400
What are they doing?

01:16:13.861 --> 01:16:15.446
Hold on.

01:16:17.031 --> 01:16:18.157
Who are they?

01:17:05.746 --> 01:17:06.997
No.

01:17:07.498 --> 01:17:08.958
Don't come this way.

01:17:46.370 --> 01:17:47.538
Se-ri?

01:19:13.666 --> 01:19:15.584
They say

01:19:16.335 --> 01:19:19.630
one sees the flashback
of the best moments in their life

01:19:19.964 --> 01:19:23.008
for a moment

01:19:23.092 --> 01:19:25.261
before they die.

01:19:27.137 --> 01:19:30.474
I think this will be

01:19:32.226 --> 01:19:34.228
one of those moments.

01:19:40.943 --> 01:19:43.862
Next year, the year after that,

01:19:44.738 --> 01:19:46.282
and even the one after that

01:19:47.741 --> 01:19:49.326
will all be good.

01:20:01.171 --> 01:20:03.090
Because I'll be thinking about you.

01:20:04.591 --> 01:20:07.052
I'll be grateful that you were born
into this world.

01:20:08.929 --> 01:20:10.556
I'll be grateful

01:20:11.265 --> 01:20:14.184
that the person I love is still breathing.

01:20:19.398 --> 01:20:20.774
Jeong Hyeok.

01:20:21.859 --> 01:20:23.027
To be honest,

01:20:24.153 --> 01:20:25.779
what you had told me

01:20:26.947 --> 01:20:28.407
was enough for me.

01:20:29.867 --> 01:20:31.160
I got to enjoy

01:20:32.202 --> 01:20:33.996
the happiness

01:20:35.164 --> 01:20:36.498
that was given to me.

01:20:38.167 --> 01:20:39.293
Se-ri...

01:20:40.044 --> 01:20:41.337
Se-ri.

01:21:38.143 --> 01:21:39.144
No.

01:21:40.020 --> 01:21:41.397
You're wrong.

01:21:41.730 --> 01:21:43.440
That wasn't enough.

01:21:45.150 --> 01:21:46.443
I still have

01:21:47.236 --> 01:21:48.862
more to say.

01:21:51.031 --> 01:21:53.117
There's something I haven't told you.

01:21:55.285 --> 01:21:56.578
I love you.

01:21:57.663 --> 01:21:59.039
I love you, Se-ri.

01:22:04.086 --> 01:22:06.797
Judging from what Man Bok has told me,

01:22:08.507 --> 01:22:10.342
you've crossed the line.

01:22:10.926 --> 01:22:14.430
You won't solve this issue
by putting your life on the line.

01:22:15.180 --> 01:22:16.557
That's what we're saying.

01:22:17.933 --> 01:22:19.309
I'm sorry to all of you.

01:22:19.977 --> 01:22:21.437
But I cannot go.

01:22:21.520 --> 01:22:25.399
-Go first and--
-We just want you to put more on the line.

01:22:25.941 --> 01:22:27.776
There's still more.

01:22:32.489 --> 01:22:33.782
You have us.

01:22:34.324 --> 01:22:37.244
We're from your troop.

01:22:37.327 --> 01:22:40.205
In our current situation,
you're as important as our country for us.

01:22:40.789 --> 01:22:42.207
Give us your orders.

01:22:44.209 --> 01:22:46.253
-I cannot do that.
-Captain Ri.

01:22:46.336 --> 01:22:47.838
Se-ri has become

01:22:48.797 --> 01:22:50.632
a valuable friend to us as well.

01:22:50.716 --> 01:22:53.135
Please give us your orders.

01:23:00.476 --> 01:23:02.019
Master Sergeant Pyo.

01:23:02.394 --> 01:23:03.437
Yes, sir.

01:23:03.645 --> 01:23:04.938
First Lieutenant Park.

01:23:05.022 --> 01:23:06.356
Yes, sir.

01:23:06.440 --> 01:23:07.774
Staff Sergeant Kim.

01:23:07.858 --> 01:23:09.902
-Yes, sir.
-Private First Class Geum.

01:23:09.985 --> 01:23:11.028
Yes, sir.

01:23:11.111 --> 01:23:12.863
Do everything in your power

01:23:13.447 --> 01:23:14.823
to protect Se-ri.

01:23:15.449 --> 01:23:16.867
That is all.

01:23:21.997 --> 01:23:22.873
I trust you.

01:24:07.334 --> 01:24:08.418
No.

01:24:10.337 --> 01:24:11.880
No.

01:24:12.548 --> 01:24:13.507
Please...

01:24:13.924 --> 01:24:14.800
Please...

01:24:15.801 --> 01:24:17.302
Please help us.

01:24:28.689 --> 01:24:30.691
Subtitle translation by Soo-ji Kim
